 is from the **Vancouver 2010 Olympic Free Dance**. Tessa Virtue and Scott Moir’s iconic white-dress free dance to “Romeo and Juliet” (by Prokofiev) is historically documented as their final and most celebrated performance at those Games. The choreography, costumes, and setting match that specific program. While the frames don’t explicitly label it “free dance,” the context (Olympic final, full-length artistic program, no compulsory elements) confirms it is the free dance segment.\n\n---\n\n✅ **Temporal sequence consistency**  \n- The frames show a continuous, uninterrupted performance sequence, with no cuts to interviews, celebrations, or other events. This reinforces that the context is purely performance-based.\n\n---\n\n✅ **Conclusion**  \nAll six criteria are met. The performance shown is unequivocally the **Free Dance** from the **Vancouver 2010 Olympics**, performed by Tessa Virtue (in white dress) and Scott Moir on an Olympic rink with branding and rings visible.\n\n**Answer: 3 (Free dance) — CORRECT.**"}, {'batch_start': 90, 'batch_end': 120, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0734.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0735.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0736.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0737.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0738.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0750.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0751.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0752.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0753.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0754.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0755.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/2LH3JCGkEBU/frames/frame_0756.jpg', '/mn